&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 8pt; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Property, plant and equipment accruals were &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;nil&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; on December 31, 2025, and 2024. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The composite depreciation rate is &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;1.82&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;% and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;0.11&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;% &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;at&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; December 31, 2025 and 2024 respectively&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; padding-left: 18pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;7.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Risk Management&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Credit Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Our principal customers for natural gas transportation services are exploration and production companies conducting business on the outer continental shelf of the Gulf of Mexico. We have concentrations of receivables from these customers throughout this region. These concentrations of customers may affect our overall credit risk in that risk factors can negatively affect the credit quality of the entire sector. Where exposed to credit risk, we analyze the customers&amp;#8217; financial condition prior to entering into an agreement, establish credit limits and monitor the appropriateness of those limits on an ongoing basis. We also obtain parental guarantees, cash deposits or letters of credit from customers to provide credit support, where appropriate, based on our financial analysis of the customer and the regulatory or contractual terms and conditions applicable to each contract.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; padding-left: 18pt; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;8.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; padding-left: 18pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Garden Banks' pro forma tax expense is reflected in its Statement of Income as tax &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;expense&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; and the related current and deferred tax liabilities (or assets) are reflected on its Comparative Balance Sheet. As the member is responsible for the taxes related to Garden Banks, in 2023 and post years income taxes are accrued in accordance with the FERC Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowance permitting the accrual of income taxes on a pass-through entity and the associated taxes accrued are treated as deemed contributions from the owners, whereas net operating loss carryovers are treated as deemed distributions. The deemed distribution recorded was $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;1,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;009,212&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; in 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; and was $&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;686,677&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; in 202&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;4&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt; and were included within Other Paid-In Capital on the Comparative Balance Sheet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
